  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -20,29 +20,7 @@ If you or your organization would like to contribute or become a sponsor, please\n \n === Bug Fixes\n \n-The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n-\n-* wssalink:2024-14[]\n-FiveCo RAP dissector infinite loop.\n-wsbuglink:20176[].\n-// cveidlink:2024-xxx[].\n-// Fixed in master: d8ca9fc339\n-// Fixed in release-4.4: 4d58fef602\n-// Fixed in release-4.2: 686dff0f01\n-// CVSS AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H\n-// CWE-835\n-// * Fuzz job crash: fuzz-2024-10-29-7320.pcap. wsbuglink:20176[].\n-\n-* wssalink:2024-15[]\n-ECMP dissector crash.\n-wsbuglink:20214[].\n-// cveidlink:2024-xxx[].\n-// Fixed in master: c8e5887073\n-// Fixed in release-4.4: 8fd60c6448\n-// Fixed in release-4.2: 06e0b0bb09\n-// CVSS AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H\n-// CWE-126\n-// * ECMP: buffer overflow detected. wsbuglink:20214[].\n+// The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n \n // * wssalink:2024-16[]\n // Foo dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n@@ -61,19 +39,6 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark grabs your ID at 3 am, goes to Waffle House, and insults people.\n \n-* JA4_c hashes an empty field to e3b0c44298fc when it should be 000000000000. wsbuglink:20066[].\n-* SRT dissector: The StreamID (SID) in the handshake extension is displayed without regarding the control characters and with NUL as terminating. wsbuglink:20113[].\n-* Ghost error message on POP3 packets. wsbuglink:20124[].\n-* Building against c-ares 1.34 fails. wsbuglink:20125[].\n-* Wi-Fi: 256 Block Ack (BA) is not parsed properly. wsbuglink:20156[].\n-* HTTP2 body decompression fails on DATA with a single padded frame. wsbuglink:20167[].\n-* SIP dissector bug due to \"be-route\" param in VIA header. wsbuglink:20173[].\n-* Coredump after trying to open 'Follow TCP stream' wsbuglink:20174[].\n-* Protobuf JSON mapping error. wsbuglink:20182[].\n-* IEEE 802.11be: Wrong regulatory info in HE Operation IE in Beacon frame. wsbuglink:20187[].\n-* Wireshark crashes when a field is dragged  from packet details towards the find input. wsbuglink:20204[].\n-* Lua DissectorTable(\"\") : set (\"10,11\") unexpected behavior in locales with comma as decimal separator. wsbuglink:20216[].\n-\n === New and Updated Features\n \n There are no new or updated features in this release.\n@@ -93,20 +58,6 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.2.8.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n-ASN.1 PER\n-ECMP\n-FiveCo RAP\n-HSRP\n-MPEG PES\n-HTTP/2\n-IEEE 802.11\n-PN-DCP\n-POP\n-ProtoBuf\n-SIP\n-SRT\n-TCP\n-UMTS RLC\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n@@ -136,6 +87,7 @@ There is no updated file format support in this release.\n This document only describes the changes introduced in Wireshark {wireshark-version}.\n You can find release notes for prior versions at the following locations:\n \n+* https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.2.9.html[Wireshark 4.2.9]\n * https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.2.8.html[Wireshark 4.2.8]\n * https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.2.7.html[Wireshark 4.2.7]\n * https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.2.6.html[Wireshark 4.2.6]\n",
